\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793804955211799001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ab9f7756-a398-486a-9acb-6cf7451644d3","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"571b-f552-5fa7-4b74"},{"link_uuid":"f7d8d8ed-3c71-4ad8-8026-27b493c6685b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d30c-f491-395f-432e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nOn 2026-11-04 a local run of the integration tier (`pytest -m integration -n 4 --dist loadgroup --max-worker-restart=0`, the second half of `make test`) on macOS at load average 25-40 failed 1 test, with 202 passed and 3 skipped in 8 min 29 s:\n\n`tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py::test_delete_permission_probe@live_reconcile_e2e` -> `AssertionError: created issue REB-6995 never became index-visible`.\n\nThis is the same symptom as the closed bug dutiable-shaded-honeyeater (`d30c-f491-395f-432e`), fixed by Gerrit 1914 (`09abac969c`), which made the visibility poll re-query Jira instead of returning a cached miss. The symptom recurs after that fix.\n\nThe test's teardown writes `leaked.log` only when the delete fails; no `leaked.log` exists for this run, so by the teardown's own accounting REB-6995 was deleted. That was not checked in Jira.\n\nA related observation: the live tests self-skip in CI, but they run, and write to the live Jira project, in any local `make test` whose environment sets `JIRA_URL`, `JIRA_USER` and `JIRA_API_TOKEN`. Agent shells on this host set all 3, so the `make verify` that AGENTS.md requires before every push creates and deletes live REB issues.\n\nDiscovered while verifying subsolar-sonorous-puppy, whose change touches only the importer and its test.\n\n## Next check\n\nTime the visibility poll on a failing run (attempts made, and elapsed time against the poll budget), and query REB-6995 read-only to confirm it is gone. That tests whether the poll is exhausting its budget under host load or is ending early.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The cause of the recurrence is identified from a timed failing run.\n- [ ] `test_delete_permission_probe` passes in the full integration tier under host load, or the tier no longer runs live-Jira writes by default in local `make test`, with the chosen behaviour recorded.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","d30c-f491-395f-432e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e55c-20d8-c5de-4ac1","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Live delete-permission probe flake recurs after the visibility-poll fix","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4d089871-0f70-469a-b616-41465dfa6f9c","ab9f7756-a398-486a-9acb-6cf7451644d3","f7d8d8ed-3c71-4ad8-8026-27b493c6685b"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793805018429303002,"uuid":"7e8d7222-2e4d-48ed-8aa0-58cb51bd1a7d"}